Below is a summary of what’s happening and two small edits to `src/js/components/Data/Data.js` that will automatically surface a “Clear Filters” button in the toolbar whenever the active filter set is non‐empty.

1. Bug scenario and root cause  
   • In your examples (Servers, Hosts, Orders, etc.) you are using the `<Data>` component with `toolbar` set (either via the `toolbar` prop or via wrapping your own `<Toolbar>`).  
   • When you interact with the search or filters controls, you expect “Clear Filters” to appear inline in that same toolbar (just like the HPE Design System Filtering pages show).  
   • Currently, `<Data>` only renders `<DataSearch/>`, `<DataView/>` and `<DataFilters/>` in its built‐in toolbar, then hands off the “clear” logic to the individual `<DataFilters/>` component — which only shows its clear button next to the filter icon, *outside* of the primary toolbar.  
   • We want to promote a single “Clear Filters” button up into the `<Toolbar>` that Data builds for you, whenever the filtered total differs from the overall total.  

2. Changes to make  
   a) import the Grommet `<Button>` in `Data.js`  
   b) after the `<DataFilters />` in the auto‐built toolbar, conditionally render a “Clear Filters” button whenever `result.filteredTotal !== result.total`

